# QA replay of the in-raid glance's plate (owner, 2026-10-19: when, what and what is kept; from its panel, Variant 1, with
# the looted container's or body's layout mirrored): the made-up readings (Rules.GlanceExample) as raid screenshots of an
# inventory screen bring them. The plate stands at the top of the map's column for 6 s, the LOOT pane mirrored in the
# desk's cells; a newer reading replaces it at once; a reading that comes while a cue is up waits for it to go; the raid's
# end takes it. Nothing on it takes a click. A developer build plays it with --dev-view --dev-script; how to run it, and
# what each still must show: glance.md beside this file. Times are in seconds.

# A --dev-view session starts on settings of its own, as at a first start, so the tour opened by itself at chapter 1
# once the data was there: it ends first.
tour end
map customs
wait 3
load
steps
start
wait 3
pos -220.21 1.07 -141.94 90
wait 6.5

# A drawer looted: its grid of three items under DRAWER, the totals over it.
glance 1
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\glance\glance-drawer

# A body, a moment later: it replaces the drawer at once, its clock anew.
glance 2
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\glance\glance-body

# 6 s after it came, the plate fades out over 0.4 s: gone.
wait 6
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\glance\glance-gone

# The extract list read, and a reading right after it: the roll call plays, the plate waits for it to go, then stands.
exits Crossroads "Trailer Park" "ZB-1013?" "Railroad Passage (Flare)"
wait 0.3
glance 1
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\glance\glance-waits
wait 8
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\glance\glance-after-cue

# The raid ends: the plate goes with it. The still waits out the RAID OVER cue (a still taken while a cue decodes or
# fades fails to render it).
end
wait 7
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\glance\glance-raid-over
exit
